1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:04,160
This whole timeline editor
is a single HTML file.

2
00:00:05,270 --> 00:00:08,680
Carry it on a stick and open it on
a machine that's never been online.

3
00:00:08,730 --> 00:00:13,893
It never uses the network. No
account, nothing to install.

4
00:00:14,123 --> 00:00:18,133
The catch: it keeps nothing when
you close it, so export your work.

5
00:00:18,183 --> 00:00:21,830
That file opens in the desktop
app and on the website too.

6
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:25,143
It's OpenChronology, free and open source.
